coder › Implemented `compareSemver(a, b)` and added tests.

## What changed

**`src/semver.ts`**
- Added a strict SemVer 2.0.0 regex parser (`parseSemver`) that validates:
  - `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` with no leading zeroes
  - optional `-prerelease` with dot-separated numeric (no leading zeroes) or alphanumeric identifiers
  - optional `+build` metadata (parsed out of the match, then ignored)
- Invalid versions throw `TypeError` with the offending string in the message, e.g. `not a semantic version: not-a-version`.
- `compareSemver` compares major/minor/patch numerically, then prereleases by the spec:
  - no prerelease > prerelease for the same core version
  - identifiers compared one by one; numeric numerically, alphanumeric lexically
  - numeric identifier < alphanumeric identifier
  - shorter identifier list is lower when all shared identifiers are equal
  - build metadata ignored

**`src/semver.test.ts`** (new)
- 22 tests covering equality, numeric-vs-lexicographic core comparison, prerelease-vs-release, numeric prerelease ordering, numeric-below-alphanumeric, the full SemVer 2.0.0 precedence chain (`alpha < alpha.1 < alpha.beta < beta < beta.2 < beta.11 < rc.1 < release`), build metadata being ignored, and `TypeError` cases (both naming the invalid string and rejecting malformed inputs like `1.0`, `01.0.0`, `1.0.0-`, `1.0.0-01`, `v1.0.0`, trailing `+`, and empty identifiers).

